415,"name":"Stephen Hogan","role":"Thomas Naylor","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/wLmVf0LGfYsgH5PNDxRGO7MlzwK.jpg"},{"id":1851218,"name":"Inga R. Kammerer","role":"Old woman","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/1ePFM4K2TJMlxCgLuCijGsXt4iu.jpg"},{"id":1851219,"name":"Annabelle Lewiston","role":"Lizzy Burns","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/eBWXJZtttiikaN2YQ5Zr0eIKUyj.jpg"},{"id":1439078,"name":"Denis Lyons","role":"James","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/7BjkR5Y90UNHvCe8QhRxn0d5sgA.jpg"},{"id":1187455,"name":"Damien Marchal","role":"Pavel Annenkov","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/riXa85JjWYBkkQQocfHxVgZQBlp.jpg"},{"id":78333,"name":"Elsa Mollien","role":"Sybille Hess","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/bocp1Bcf3wZLNJezr086ahKehZF.jpg"},{"id":1449965,"name":"Torsten Ranft","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/y7sJbVwcHLfod0G1jm4pttfhigt.jpg"},{"id":45268,"name":"Jürgen Rißmann","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/yvPTXv2kqVN7fQHjAAnJEtH3bwi.jpg"},{"id":50792,"name":"Henning Peker","role":"Stirner","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/vAtZTarZEr2q4mkDdaNBsYpsZTA.jpg"},{"id":4757014,"name":"Djigui Diarra"}],"crew":[],"videos":[],"watchProviders":[],"episodeGroups":[],"translations":[{"language":"it-IT","title":"Il giovane Karl Marx","overview":"Alla metà del Diciannovesimo secolo l'Europa è in fermento. In Inghilterra, Francia e Germania i lavoratori scendono in piazza per protestare contro le durissime condizioni nelle fabbriche, e gli intellettuali partecipano come possono all'opposizione. Uno di loro, il tedesco Karl Marx, a soli 26 anni è costretto a rifugiarsi a Parigi insieme alla moglie Jenny. Qui Karl conosce un suo coetaneo, Friedrich Engels, che, nonostante provenga da una ricca famiglia di industriali, simpatizza con le sue idee rivoluzionarie. Superate le prime resistenze, fra i due ragazzi nasce una solida amicizia che li porterà a conquistarsi la stima dei capi dei movimenti dei lavoratori. Fino a diventarne leader a loro volta.","tagline":"La rivoluzione è giovane"},{"language":"en-US","title":"The Young Karl Marx","overview":"26 year-old Karl Marx embarks with his wife, Jenny, on the road to exile. In 1844 in Paris, he meets Friedrich Engels, an industrialist’s son, who has been investigating the sordid birth of the British working class. Engels, the dandy, provides the last piece of the puzzle to the young Karl Marx’s new vision of the world. Together, between censorship and the police’s repression, riots and political upheavals, they will lead the labor movement during its development into a modern era."},{"language":"fr-FR","overview":"Europe, 1844-1848. En Allemagne, une opposition intellectuelle en pleine ébullition est fortement réprimée. En France, les ouvriers du Faubourg Saint-Antoine se sont mis en marche. En Angleterre aussi, le peuple est dans la rue, la révolution là-bas est industrielle. À 26 ans, Karl Marx entraine sa femme Jenny sur les routes de l'exil. Il parvient à Paris où il rencontre Friedrich Engels, fils d'un grand industriel, qui a étudié les conditions de travail du prolétariat anglais. Ces deux fils de famille, brillants, insolents et drôles, vont parvenir à fédérer un mouvement révolutionnaire et forger les outils théoriques propres à émanciper, par delà les frontières de l'Europe, les peuples opprimés du monde entier."}],"images":{"logos":[],"posters":[],"backdrops":[]},"poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/kvAXa0hNJQVzgIdPg0Vn0kJzDyM.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/uJSuJ4eocpofYc6LjEJ7G3vgbfS.jpg","seasons":[],"schema":{}}},"artworkLibrary":{"tmdb":{"schemaVersion":1,"source":"tmdb","id":400020,"type":"movie","originalLanguage":"fr-FR","series":{"poster":{"it":{"status":"available","selected":{"type":"poster","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/kvAXa0hNJQVzgIdPg0Vn0kJzDyM.jpg","previewUrl":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/kvAXa0hNJQVzgIdP